  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nHigh pressure has settled south of New England, and will slowly\ndrift off the Eastern Seaboard today. This brings a moderating \ntrend on southwesterly flow, with highs warming into the mid 60s\nin many spots today. Temps warm further on Monday, with highs \npushing into the upper 60s, and even low 70s in a few spots.\n\nA weak cold front crosses through during the day on Monday, \nbringing only the chance for a few showers across the north. \nOtherwise, the front merely serves to usher in the next ridge of\nhigh pressure, which brings a cooler Canadian airmass with it. \nHighs fall back into the 40s and 50s for Tuesday and Wednesday, \nbut then moderate back into the 60s again for late in the week \nas the high moves offshore.\n\nThe next front likely crosses on Friday, and has the chance to \nbring a few showers to more of the area, but nothing of \nsignificance. Behind this front, the next ridge of high pressure\narrives just in time for next weekend.",
